WEBVTT

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:01.579
In the ontology interface, you can

00:00:01.579 --> 00:00:04.059
document inventory risk as a specific

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:06.559
multivariable condition. You write

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:08.039
out that risk occurs when a

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:09.839
product's position is expected to fall

00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:11.559
below its required historical buffer

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:13.819
before the next scheduled replenishment

00:00:13.819 --> 00:00:15.779
arrives. Okay, so you type out

00:00:15.779 --> 00:00:17.419
that logic in natural language.

00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:19.099
Then what happens?

00:00:19.239 --> 00:00:21.039
Does the AI just magically know

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:22.079
how to execute that?

00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:24.059
No, writing it is just the

00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:27.419
first step. Then you explicitly Mathematically

00:00:27.419 --> 00:00:29.199
link that written rule to both

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.519
the store entity and the inventory

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:32.859
entity in your model.

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:34.119
What is linking it?

00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:36.139
Actually do by forging that link

00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:37.819
you make the rule discoverable to

00:00:37.819 --> 00:00:40.179
any downstream AI agent consuming the

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:41.958
ontology. So when
